ople’s freedom, many people will balk.","然而如果这些系统严重侵犯了人们的自由的话，许多人将会停滞不前。"]],"sedition":[["Trade Union leaders were charged with sedition.","工会领导人被控犯有煽动罪。"]],"overwork":[["You’ve been overworking – why don’t you take a week off?","你最近在超强度工作——为什么不休息一周呢？"]],"bombast":[["There was no bombast or conceit in his speech.","他的发言里没有浮夸或自负。"]],"biased":[["Of course I’m biased, but I thought my daughter’s paintings were the best.","当然我有偏心，但我还是认为我女儿的画最好。"]],"perceptive":[["He was one of the most perceptive U.S. political commentators.","他曾是美国最具洞察力的政治评论员之一。"]],"genome":[["Even so, the platypus genome reveals the animal held onto genes for odor-detection.","尽管如此，鸭嘴兽的基因组还显示其带有气味感觉的基因。"]],"furlough":[["During his furlough, he studied for a teaching qualification.","暂时停工休假期间，他为取得教师资格而学习。"]],"bridle":[["The metal mouthpiece of a bridle, serving to control, curb, and direct an animal.","马勒， 嚼子放在嘴里的金属制马勒，用于控制约束和驾御牲畜。"]],"enrage":[["Many readers were enraged by his article.","许多读者被他的文章激怒了。"]],"birthright":[["Freedom of speech is every American’s birthright.","言论自由是每一个美国人与生俱来的权利。"]],"accusation":[["Burton’s enemies had made false accusations against him.","伯顿的敌人对他提出不实的指责。"]],"immoral":[["It’s immoral to be rich while people are starving and homeless.","不管别人忍饥挨饿、居无定所而自己发家致富是不道德的。"]],"farcical":[["Opposition leaders described the government’s plans as ‘farcical’.","反对党领导人说政府的计划就像“一场闹剧”。"]],"linguist":[["He had a scholarly air and was an accomplished linguist.","他有一种学者的风度，而且是个熟练掌握多国语言的人。"]],"assuage":[["Nothing could assuage his guilt.","什么都不能减轻他的内疚。"]],"transcribe":[["He had been asked to transcribe an ancient manuscript.","他被要求抄写一本古代手稿。"]],"indefinitely":[["The project has been postponed indefinitely.","这项工程被无限期延期。"]],"coax":[["‘Please, Vic, come with us,’ Nancy coaxed.","“求你了，维克，跟我们一起去吧。”南希哄劝道。"]],"sensual":[["The poem captures the sensual pleasure of walking barefoot on grass.","这首诗描绘了赤脚踏过草地时感官上的愉悦。"]],"censorship":[["But for those undaunted, here's our guide to circumventing internet cen